00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.230 align:start position:0%
the two days summit in the ethiopian  capital concluded with a call for  greater african representation on the  global stage  seventy years after the creation of the  united nations au leaders complained  that africa was still unrepresented on  the u.n security council  they are demanding at least two  prominent and five non-permanent seats  it is the right time  to reform and revitalize the united  nations system to reflect  current global realities and ensure that  it is a more representative and  equitable body  only fair representation  and transparency in those institutions  can usher in a just era in  multilateralism  the past 18 months have been chaotic for  africa with crews in chad guinea malibu  nafaso and sudan  as well as the protracted civil war here  in ethiopia  the eu has been accused of an  inconsistent response notably by not  suspending chad from the 55-member  organization after the military took  over following the death of long-time  leader idris debbie  every african  leader  in the assembly  has condemned  unequivocally  the  pattern of the resurgence of the cycle  or the wave  of unconstitutional changes of  government  the african union's efforts to combat  the covet 19 pandemic were also  discussed at length after a long delay  african nations began receiving larger  donations of covet 19 magazines in  november but the continent is still far  behind global vaccination targets partly  due to what some say are logistical  challenges  governments now hope the au's creation  of a continent-wide drug regulator the  african medicine's agency helps them  roll out vaccines to catch up with other  parts of the world  and differences between members over the  union's relationship with israel broke  into the open  palestinian prime minister muhammad  shitai made an impassioned plea to  leaders to reconsider their decision to  give israel observer status at au  meetings we believe that granting israel  observer status at the african union is  undeserved reward this actually  a reward that encourages israel to  continue violating international  treaties breaching all agreements with  us  the prime minister was supported by some  important member states including  nigeria and south africa whose ruling  party the african national congress  supports the palestinian cause  in the end the palestinian argument was  worn and leaders agreed to suspend  israel's observer status  muhammad al-jazeera addison
 

